{"title":"2005 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are two values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> for which the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/2/782a7d47e8f237b0150c0a449b6144e2521d2736.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4x^2 + ax + 8x + 9 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"175\" height=\"16\" /> has only one solution for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. What is the sum of those values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/b/91b0806219d1316909582a85033c952996e1f319.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } -16 \\qquad\\textbf{(B) } -8 \\qquad\\textbf{(C) } 0 \\qquad\\textbf{(D) } 8 \\qquad\\textbf{(E) } 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"418\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A quadratic equation has exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> distinct root if and only if the left-hand side is a perfect square. So we require\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/e/aee99e4c1e6765f6f6700fab2123e2e46c37c2f2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4x^2 + ax + 8x + 9 = (mx + n)^2 = m^2 x^2 + 2mnx + n^2.\\]\" width=\"425\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Two polynomials are equal only if their coefficients are equal, so we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/d/0fde2fffe713eab8e07d2455b22388cd837d2e93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m^2 = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"59\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/4/cc4b0e18ed551d83b1a5a99a3fd0cf422f946388.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2 = 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"54\" height=\"17\" />, which reduce to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/3/663a24e30b90fa677eaf8bb530fad5efc8425f16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = \\pm 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"65\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/f/f2faf118d0819a7e08df6da482e1a9a3e1c3b411.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = \\pm 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"60\" height=\"15\" /> respectively. By equating <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-coefficients, it follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/4/bc46a724caece5e30832233f285eeb0f6422f6eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + 8 = 2mn = \\pm 2 \\cdot 2\\cdot 3 = \\pm 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"251\" height=\"15\" />, so either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/b/c4b38cdab3d38c76e3fe6b2e0734b43a88b1c39d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 12-8 = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"119\" height=\"15\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/4/bb4e4d4c93159ce7646143da04112f43ba0c0773.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = -12-8 = -20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"156\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Accordingly, the desired sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/d/4ed5d7e2d759404c0031fb47cbd811841c94e1c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4+(-20) = \\boxed{\\textbf{(A) } -16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"191\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>(Alternatively, we can observe that whatever the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> are, they must lead to equations of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/e/f3e3f32e250994f6ef7b7c8d42d891c25cd2d8df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$px^2 + qx + r = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"134\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/6/706765780ad6c688c085634a7b5681c4a826f9c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$px^2 - qx + r = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"133\" height=\"18\" />, corresponding to the perfect squares <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/5/4e527b1d1cd19323826c2e74d6e1a40113bd5c8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(mx \\pm n\\right)^2 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"116\" height=\"23\" />. So the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> choices of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, say <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/9/5e97a8af68fbc8e357d3ee0eba452022b06c1875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />, must satisfy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/9/ce9d7f5c05fae544efe5a8ef80ea27942ee455f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1 + 8 = q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"81\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/5/755f79d18e50b54afd5389f1dd03e97d914e16af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2 + 8 = -q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"95\" height=\"16\" />, and adding these equations yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/0/c60f503e975875429d0238e214342eac0e8becc0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1 + a_2 + 16 = 0 \\iff a_1 + a_2 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(A) } -16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"353\" height=\"30\" />.)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since this quadratic must have a double root, its discriminant must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Therefore we require\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/3/a53510911ccaa1f859dbdc3616f27dca7e5a1f15.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(a+8)^2 - 4 \\cdot 4 \\cdot  9 = 0 \\iff a^2 + 16a - 80 = 0.\\]\" width=\"368\" height=\"20\" /> At this point, Vieta's formulae directly give the sum of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/e/77e3d265a58d08dba1f5430fa6d7b301a7c85f6e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\frac{16}{1} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(A) } -16}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"155\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>(Alternatively, we could use the quadratic formula to directly solve this equation for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />; the precise value of the expression under the square root does not actually matter, as it will cancel out due to the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/2/91205e81c98c486418902c88d5c396f5355491f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pm$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" /> signs when added. This again gives the required sum as\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/2/c725d1fa1565a357e72fe94b727a5b23323a8a74.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{-16 + \\sqrt{\\text{something}}}{2} + \\frac{-16 - \\sqrt{\\text{something}}}{2} = \\frac{-32}{2} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(A) } -16}.)\\]\" width=\"498\" height=\"39\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A\">2005 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_10_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 10 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 10 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017192100\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.050 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.068 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 278/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2322/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 156/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6790/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   14.536      1 -total\n 57.93%    8.420      1 Template:AMC10_box\n 40.94%    5.951      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:3710:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017192100 and revision id 253059. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}